        "problem": "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{x^2 - x + 1}[/math]}} \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+0x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}-x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{x + 64}[/math]}} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x+1}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,63\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^2$-term and the $x$-term. So, we write it using zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\nx^3+{\\color{red}0}x^2 + {\\color{red}0}x + 64\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-x+1 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+0x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}-x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x+1}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,63\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\qquad$ $x^2 - x + 1\\quad$ and $\\quad x + 64.$",
        "screenshot": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054087/example-5033.png"
      }
